    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0176" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg134"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 478.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 14, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch (No. 304) of the 23d ultimo, relative to your calling Earl Russell’s
                    attention to an instance during the Crimean war, in which it seems that Great
                    Britain demanded the restitution of a vessel in circumstances similar, to those
                    which belong to the case of the Emily St. Pierre, and to inform you that your
                    proceedings, as therein stated, are approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
